{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And what shall one answer.</b> Every messenger of the messengers of every nation — this one shall answer: for YHWH has founded Zion, and the king of Assyria cannot prevail against it. And the meaning of <b>and what shall one answer</b> is that the nations will ask what has happened to Jerusalem, and likewise the messengers shall answer those who sent them:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra reads מלאך as 'messenger' rather than 'ambassador'; the bracketed editorial note [צ\"ל יענו] corrects the verb יענה to plural יענו, 'they shall answer.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:53.693863331Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}